<title>USA: Entergy Corp denies mulling Yorkshire bid.</title>
<headline>Entergy Corp denies mulling Yorkshire bid.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entergy Corp on Monday denied a published report that it was considering a possible bid for Yorkshire Electricity Plc.  </p>
<p>Entergy is working with British Petroleum Co Plc to develop a power plant near Yorkshire, and earlier this year the New Orleans-based company created an office in Britain, said company spokesman Patrick Sweeney.</p>
<p>Sweeney said Entergy is not considering a friendly bid of about 1.3 bln stg for Yorkshire, as reported by the London Sunday Telegraph.</p>
<p>He said that to his knowledge, Entergy officials have not met with any Yorkshire Electricity officials in any acquisition talks.</p>
